{"id":257840510624065,"type":"artist","name":"Bill Monroe","artist":null,"year":null,"weight":11,"info":{"img":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/MonroeBrothers_%28cropped%29.jpg?width=500","bio":"William Smith Monroe (Jerusalem Ridge, Kentucky 1911-Springfield, Tennessee 1996). Cantante country inventor del estilo \"bluegrass\". Desde niño domina la mandolina. En 1938 graba su canción más famosa \"The Mule Skinner Blues\". Con su banda The Blue Grass Boys crea un estilo musical tan innovador que nadie sabe cómo llamarlo. Su canción \"Blue Moon of Kentucky\" es el primer single de Elvis Presley. Con la aparición de la música folk, su fama aumenta, tocando en todas las universidades americanas.","tags":["bluegrass","country","folk","americana","Traditional Country"]},"works":[{"id":98950740267675,"type":"song","name":"Kentucky Waltz","artist":"Bill Monroe","year":1933,"weight":6,"yt":"RAnOnmUbvyc","src":"books","from":{"books":[{"name":"Scaruffi","title":"A History of Rock Music 1951-2000 (Piero Scaruffi)"}],"podcasts":[],"lists":[],"n_lists":0}},{"id":6779152621276,"type":"album","name":"Knee Deep in Blue Grass","artist":"Bill Monroe","year":1958,"weight":7,"yt":"bZLSOmeNkfg","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":59502452022900,"name":"RYM Top — Folk — Traditional Country","rank":62,"scaruffi":null},{"id":60739539139006,"name":"RYM Top — Folk — Traditional Bluegrass","rank":15,"scaruffi":null},{"id":276702392435984,"name":"RYM Top — Country — Bluegrass","rank":127,"scaruffi":null}],"n_lists":3}},{"id":214886791866728,"type":"album","name":"I Saw the Light","artist":"Bill Monroe","year":1959,"weight":9,"yt":"BBXwQ0Y4sec","src":"musthear","from":{"books":[],"podcasts":[],"lists":[{"id":29400011212191,"name":"RYM Top — Folk — Bluegrass Gospel","rank":2,"scaruffi":null},{"id":59502452022900,"name":"RYM Top — Folk — Traditional Country","rank":93,"scaruffi":null},{"id":60739539139006,"name":"RYM Top — Folk — Traditional Bluegr